From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000059 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: Reserve rgb9e5 for the Metal standard library

STEAMAC-A9 retains a user-defined float4 rgb9e5(thread const uint&) and
its call at lines 163/289. Metal's stdlib also exports the rgb9e5<T>
pixel-type alias. With using namespace metal, lookup of the unqualified
call is ambiguous, even though the competing declaration is not a
function. The illegal-function-name set did not include that type name.

Reserve rgb9e5 through the existing function/entry-point renaming path,
so definitions and calls retain the user's unpacking implementation.
The rgb9e5_helper compute regression checks zero, normal and maximum
RGB9E5 values after nested user helper calls.
---
 spirv_msl.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -19524,6 +19524,7 @@ const std::unordered_set<std::string> &CompilerMSL::get_illegal_func_names()
 		"vertex",
 		"kernel",
 		"log10",
+		"rgb9e5",
 		"saturate",
 		"assert",
 		"fmin3",
